In message <200212141319.36714.rupp@chello.at>
	so spake Wolfgang Rupp (rupp):

> I installed 3.2 on my DEC3000-400. The machine is switched to serial
> console (and does not even have a graphics card).
> 
> If I boot single user, I can log in. If I boot multiuser, I can see
> the boot messages on the Terminal, up to the date when the machine
> started all daemons. Then the terminal stops responding. Just dead.
> 
> Has anybody seen this before? Any ideas?

You need to boot single user and edit /etc/ttys.  Change the line:
    console "/usr/libexec/getty std.9600"   vt220 off  secure
to:
    console "/usr/libexec/getty std.9600"   vt220 on  secure

Ie: replace the "off" with "on" in that line.

 - todd

